-- title:
--   Special-fibre points of the rigid chart as level structures
-- statement:
--   Throughout, $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ denotes `AlgebraicClosure ℚ`.
--
--   **Data at $q$.** A prime $q$ with $5\le q$, a non-zero natural number $M'$ with $q\nmid M'$, and a valuation subring $A$ of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ satisfying `A.LiesOverPrime q`, i.e. $q$ is a non-unit of $A$. Further: a finite set $W$ of places of the field `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'` (the subfield of the Laurent series over the residue field of $A$ obtained by adjoining $j$ and its $M'$-th transform, `IntermediateField.adjoin K {jqModC K, jqNModC K N}`) over the residue field of $A$, together with `hW`, which says that $W$ is exactly the set `ssPlaces q M' (ResidueField A)` of places $w$ with `IsSupersingularPlace q M' (ResidueField A) w`; the inclusion `hle` of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` (the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-subfield of the Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ generated by the image of the full level-$M'$ modular function field) in `fieldBar q M'` $=$ `xHFunctionFieldBar (q^2*M') (levelH q M')`, where `levelH q M'` is the kernel of the reduction $(\mathbb Z/q^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q)^\times$; a constant reduction $R_0$ of $A$ from `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` to `modularFunctionFieldC (ResidueField A) M'`, that is, a valuation subring $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ of the source, a surjective residue homomorphism $R_0.\mathrm{residue}$ onto the target with kernel the maximal ideal, a map on places preserving degree, and the compatibilities with $A$, with scaling and with push-forward of divisors recorded in the fields of `ConstantReduction`; the hypothesis `hR₀`, which states that the coefficientwise image under $A\hookrightarrow\overline{\mathbb Q}$ of any Laurent series $y$ with coefficients in $A$, if it lies in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'`, lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$ and its $R_0$-residue, read as a Laurent series over the residue field of $A$, is the coefficientwise reduction of $y$; and a chosen element $s\in W$, i.e. a supersingular place.
--
--   **The small field and its valuation ring.** An intermediate field $k_0$ of $\mathbb Q$ in $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ and an element $\pi_0\in k_0$ whose image lies in $A$. Write $A_0:=$ `A.comap (algebraMap k₀ Q̄)` for the induced valuation ring of $k_0$ and $\kappa:=$ `ResidueField A₀`. The hypotheses on these are: $A_0$ is a discrete valuation ring, its maximal ideal is the ideal generated by $\pi_0$, $A_0$ is a henselian local ring, $\kappa$ is algebraically closed, and `hκ`: every $a\in A$ admits $c\in k_0$ with image in $A$ such that $a-c$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$.
--
--   **Auxiliary prime and rigid level field.** A prime $\ell'$ with $\ell'\ne q$, $3\le\ell'$ and $\ell'\nmid M'$; an element $\xi\in k_0$ which is a primitive $(q\ell')$-th root of unity, together with `hιξ`: some ring homomorphism $\iota:k_0\to\mathbb C$ sends $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell'))$; an intermediate field $K$ of $k_0$ in the Laurent series over $k_0$ with `hK` saying that $K$ is the base change to $k_0$ of `xHFunctionField ((q*ℓ')^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ') M')`, the function field of the modular curve of level $(q\ell')^2M'$ with $H$ the kernel of $(\mathbb Z/(q\ell')^2M')^\times\to(\mathbb Z/q\ell')^\times$; an $A_0$-algebra structure on $K$ forming a scalar tower with $k_0$; and an element $j\in K$ whose Laurent series is the image of `jq` under `coeffEmb k₀`, with $j\ne 0$.
--
--   **Moduli-theoretic input over $A_0$.** The variable-change rules `hℓ` (for every $A_0$-algebra $T$, Weierstrass curve $W$ over $T$, variable change $C$ and level datum $D=(x_P,y_P,x_Q,y_Q)$: if $D$ is a Katz level-$\ell'$ structure on $W$ — both points satisfy the affine equation, both abscissae are roots of `W.preΨ ℓ'`, and the two independence elements are units — then `D.variableChange C` is one on $C\bullet W$) and `hM` (likewise `IsGamma0PowAt W p k h`, i.e. `W.IsTwoKernel h` when $p^k=2$ and `W.IsCyclicGenKernel p k h` otherwise, is preserved on passing to $C\bullet W$ and `kernelVariableChangeDeg C (gamma0PowDeg p k) h`); a family $\mathcal G$ of relative group laws on projective Weierstrass models with unit discriminant over $A_0$-algebras, with the chord–tangent property `h𝒢` (existence of a points-evaluation for each model) and the origin property `h𝒢O` (existence of an origin chart section with vanishing $x/y$ and $z/y$); a level transport datum $\mathcal T$ for $\mathcal G$ at $q$ satisfying `IsSectionTransport` (two clauses, for variable changes and for coefficient maps, asserting that the transported sections pull back to the original ones along the realising graded maps); and the realisation hypotheses `hVC` and `hCO`, asserting for all $A_0$-algebras, projective Weierstrass models, variable changes and $A_0$-algebra maps the existence of a graded ring homomorphism of the graded coordinate rings `projModelGradingCR`, subject to the inclusion of irrelevant ideals, which is a variable-change homomorphism, respectively a coefficient homomorphism, in the sense of `IsVariableChangeHom` and `IsCoefficientHom`.
--
--   Write $C:=$ [`AlgebraicCurve.TwoChartIntegralModel.chartAlgFin A₀ K j`](def/AlgebraicCurve_TwoChartIntegralModel.html#L142), the $A_0$-subalgebra `chartAlg A₀ K {j}` of $K$, and let
--   $$\mathcal Y:=\{\,y\subseteq C \text{ an ideal}\ \mid\ y \text{ maximal and } \pi_0\in y\,\}$$
--   (the image of $\pi_0$ under `algebraMap A₀ C` lies in $y$). Write $R:=$ `rigidDataPow A₀ ℓ' M' q hℓ hM 𝒢 𝒯` for the rigid Weierstrass datum obtained from the product of the $\Gamma_0$-power component at $M'$, the level-$\ell'$ component and the Drinfeld level component at $q$; an element of $R.\mathrm{Raw}\,\kappa$ consists of a Weierstrass curve over $\kappa$ with unit discriminant, a level datum whose three slots are the $\Gamma_0(M')$-datum `level.1`, a `LevelPData κ` given by four coordinates `level.2.1`, and a `RawDrinfeldPair κ` (a projective model with two sections) `level.2.2`, together with the assertion that this datum is a level structure on the curve. Points of $R.\mathrm{Pt}\,\kappa$ are classes of raw data modulo the relation generated by variable changes.
--
--   **Alignment condition.** For $y\in\mathcal Y$ let $\mathrm{Al}(y)$ denote the following condition. For every Laurent series $g$ over $\mathbb Q$ lying in `modularFunctionFieldFull M'`, whose image $\bar g$ in `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` lies in $R_0.\mathrm{integers}$, such that (i) for every place $P$ of `modularFunctionFieldBar M'` over $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, $0\le P.\mathrm{ord}$ of the image of `jq` implies $0\le P.\mathrm{ord}(\bar g)$, and (ii) $R_0.\mathrm{residue}(\bar g)$ lies in the valuation subring of the place $s$: whenever the image of $g$ under `coeffEmb k₀` followed by the substitution $q\mapsto q^{\ell'}$ (`qExpand k₀ ℓ'`) lies in $K$ and the resulting element of $K$ lies in $C$, then for every $c\in k_0$ whose image lies in $A$ and whose residue in the residue field of $A$ equals $s.\mathrm{evalAt}(R_0.\mathrm{residue}(\bar g))$, the difference in $C$ of that element and the image of $c$ under `algebraMap A₀ C` lies in $y$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** There exists a map $\Phi:\mathcal Y\to R.\mathrm{Raw}\,\kappa$ such that the following four assertions hold.
--
--   1.
--
--   For every $y\in\mathcal Y$ satisfying $\mathrm{Al}(y)$, every point $P$ of the affine curve of $\Phi(y)$ over $\kappa$ with $q\cdot P=0$ is zero; that is, the curve of $\Phi(y)$ has no non-trivial $q$-torsion over $\kappa$.
--
--   2.
--
--   For all $y,y'\in\mathcal Y$ satisfying $\mathrm{Al}(y)$ and $\mathrm{Al}(y')$ respectively, there is a variable change $C_0$ over $\kappa$ such that the $R$-action of $C_0$ on $\Phi(y)$ has the same curve as $\Phi(y')$, the same $\Gamma_0(M')$-slot `level.1` as $\Phi(y')$, and the same value of the Weil pairing in the level-$\ell'$ slot: with the elliptic structure on the curve of $\Phi(y')$ supplied by the unit discriminant of $\Phi(y')$, the pairing `weilPairing0` of that curve over $\kappa$ at $\ell'$, evaluated on the two points of the base change to $\kappa$ obtained by `LevelRelabelling.toPoint` from the coordinates $(x_P,y_P)$ and $(x_Q,y_Q)$ of the level-$\ell'$ slot of $C_0\cdot\Phi(y)$, equals the same pairing evaluated on the points obtained from the coordinates of the level-$\ell'$ slot of $\Phi(y')$.
--
--   3.
--
--   For every $\gamma\in\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ lying in $\Gamma(q)$ and in $\Gamma_0(M')$ there exist $\gamma'\in\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$, again lying in $\Gamma(q)$ and in $\Gamma_0(M')$, and a $k_0$-algebra automorphism $\tau$ of $K$ such that: `IsLevelAutAt k₀ (q*ℓ') ξ (q*ℓ') ((q*ℓ')^2*M') (levelH (q*ℓ') M') γ'⁻¹ K τ` holds, i.e. for every weight $k$, every pair $f,g$ of modular forms of that weight for $\Gamma_H((q\ell')^2M')$ with integral $q$-expansions $p_f,p_g$, $p_g$ having non-zero associated series over $\mathbb Q$, every $x\in K$ whose Laurent series is the image of $p_f/p_g$ and every ring homomorphism $\iota:k_0\to\mathbb C$ carrying $\xi$ to $\exp(2\pi i/(q\ell'))$, the $\iota$-image of the Laurent series of $\tau x$ times the $q$-expansion of $g\mid_k\mathrm{conjElemN}(q\ell')\gamma'^{-1}$ equals the $q$-expansion of $f\mid_k\mathrm{conjElemN}(q\ell')\gamma'^{-1}$; moreover $\tau$ maps $C$ into $C$; and for all $y,y_1\in\mathcal Y$ such that $b\in y\iff\tau b\in y_1$ for every $b\in C$ with $\tau b\in C$, and for all raw data $x,x_1\in R.\mathrm{Raw}\,\kappa$ and every proof that the discriminant of the curve of the Drinfeld slot of $x$ is a unit, the following implication holds: if the class of $x$ in $R.\mathrm{Pt}\,\kappa$ equals the class of $\Phi(y)$, and $x_1$ has the same curve as $x$, the same $\Gamma_0(M')$-slot as $x$, level-$\ell'$ slot equal to `LevelPData.relabel` of that of $x$ by the integral matrix of $\gamma$ (replacing the pair of points by the $\gamma$-linear combinations formed with the affine group law), and Drinfeld slot equal to `RawDrinfeldPair.relabel 𝒢` of that of $x$ by the same matrix (the corresponding $\mathbb Z$-linear combinations of the two sections for the group law $\mathcal G$), then the class of $\Phi(y_1)$ in $R.\mathrm{Pt}\,\kappa$ equals the class of $x_1$.
--
--   4.
--
--   For all $y,y'\in\mathcal Y$ such that $y'$ satisfies $\mathrm{Al}(y')$: if the classes of $\Phi(y)$ and $\Phi(y')$ in $R.\mathrm{Pt}\,\kappa$ coincide, then $y=y'$. (The alignment condition is imposed on $y'$ only.)
--
--   This is the dictionary between the closed points of the special fibre of the $j$-finite chart of the rigid level-$q\ell'$ integral model and full-level structures over the algebraically closed residue field $\kappa$: a point of the fibre aligned with the supersingular place $s$ gives a Weierstrass curve with $\Gamma_0(M')$-, level-$\ell'$- and Drinfeld $\Gamma(q)$-data whose $q$-torsion over $\kappa$ vanishes, such data are determined up to a single variable change and have a well-defined Weil pairing in the $\ell'$-slot, the $\Gamma(q)\cap\Gamma_0(M')$-relabellings are realised by automorphisms of $K$ preserving the chart algebra, and distinct aligned points give distinct moduli classes. It is used in the construction of level automorphisms matching prescribed closed points of the chart, where it is cited by [`ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_isLevelAutAt_map_chartAlgFin_eq_of_over_of_over_of_not_dvd`](thm.html#ModularCurve.FullLevel.exists_isLevelAutAt_map_chartAlgFin_eq_of_over_of_over_of_not_dvd).
